==Enemy==
Daboo of the Dead is truly a monstrous threat, with a whopping '''3 million HP''', '''30,000 damage''' along with a massive [[Omni Strike]] range of '''800''' and a '''10-second slow effect'''. On top of that, he even has immunities to almost every debuff you can think of (Freeze/Slow/Knockback/Weaken). Unlike most other [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], he cannot burrow past your cats, yet he still revives with 10% HP an unlimited number of times.

==Strategy==
Since his slow effect has almost 100% uptime, any unit he can knock back in one hit will likely be unable to ever reach Daboo, instead allowing him to chain attacks on them until they die. For this reason and due to how few units can outrange him, it is recommended to use [[:Category:Cats with Slow ability|slow-immune units]], fast units and tanky units above all; the more of these attributes, the better.

Meatshields that work great include [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], boosted [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]]. A stack of Shigongs can absolutely take out Daboo, provided you have other units to deal with the non-[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] peons.

[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera Cat]] work well against him too, being able to block him and damage him for a relatively long time. The problem usually comes in doing that while also dealing with whatever supports him, meaning that units should be picked with his supporters in mind, such as [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] in [[Parade of the Dead (Deadly)|Parade of the Dead]]/[[Prisoner's Progress (Merciless)|Prisoner's Progress]], [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]] in [[March to Death (Merciless)|March to Death]], [[King Wahwah]] as well as the nasty [[:Category:Red Enemies|Reds]] in [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 46|Heavenly Tower Floor 46]], and [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]] in [[Rank-Up Test 2 (Rank 12)|Catclaw Championships Rank 12, Test 2]].

Although Daboo is able to revive indefinitely, it generally isn't concerning due to how he is fought, not even factoring in the fact that he can only revive with 10% HP. Nevertheless, having a high-leveled [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] is always optimal, as despite being unable to freeze him, its max health percentage-based damage values can consistently whittle him at range every minute or so, which can be all the difference you make in each battle. A level 20 Holyblast can even Z-kill Daboo's corpse because it has [[Soulstrike]].

